# Stack: Python

Python >= [[ python_version ]] with uv: always `uv run`, never `pip install` or activate the venv. Done = code + tests + wiki.

- **Design records:** `docs/design/NNNN-*.md` from `0000-template.md`, a line in its `README.md` index (read only what it names). New feature, dependency or public interface (config keys, CLI, HTTP API, file formats): write one first.
- Never re-propose `TODO.md`'s "Decided against".

## Don't read

`uv.lock` (use `uv tree --depth 1`), `CHANGELOG.md` (use `git log`), `.venv/`, `htmlcov/`, `.coverage`, `.mypy_cache/`, `.ruff_cache/`, `.pytest_cache/`; generated wiki blocks (`<!-- generated:start/end -->`)[% if kind == 'service' %], `docs/openapi.json`[% endif %].

## Commands

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Install / add | `uv sync` / `uv add <pkg>` (dev: `--dev`) |
| Lint, format | `uv run ruff check --fix`, `uv run ruff format` (also the `python` code blocks in `*.md`: design records' sketches too) |
| Types (strict) | `uv run mypy` |
| Tests (80% floor) / integration | `uv run pytest` / `RUN_INTEGRATION=1 uv run pytest -m integration --no-cov` |
| Wiki sections[% if kind == 'service' %], `docs/openapi.json`[% endif %] | `uv run scripts/gen-wiki.py` |
[% if has_cli %]
| Run | `uv run [[ project_name ]] --help` |
[% endif %]

## Repository map

| Path | What |
|---|---|
[% if stdlib_only %]
| `src/[[ package_name ]]/[[ package_name ]].py` | The program: stdlib only, runs as `python3 -IS`; argparse by default; a hand parser is fine, as nothing template-owned imports the parser. `__init__`, `__main__` are for `uv run` |
[% else %]
| `src/[[ package_name ]]/` | The package[% if has_cli %]: `config.py`, `cli.py` (Typer)[% endif %][% if kind == 'service' %], `api.py` (FastAPI)[% endif %] |
[% endif %]
| `tests/unit/`, `tests/integration/` | pytest; integration is marked and opt-in |
| `docs/wiki/`, `docs/design/` | The wiki (`.standard.toml`, T); design records |
| `docs/ai/` | Prompts, review checklist (T) |
| `contrib/` | `system-packages.txt` (apt `build:`/`runtime:`)[% if contrib %]; [[ contrib | join(', ') ]][% endif %] |
[% if container_image %]
| `Dockerfile` | Image (T skeleton) |
[% endif %]
| `CHANGELOG.md`, `pyproject.toml` version, `.release-please-manifest.json` | release-please only |

## Conventions

- **Types:** full annotations, `mypy --strict`. A `# type: ignore` or `noqa` states its reason.
- **Style:** ruff (line length 100). Comments say *why*. No `print`: `logging`[% if has_cli %]; only the CLI writes stdout (`[[ 'sys.stdout.write' if stdlib_only else 'typer.echo' ]]`)[% endif %].
[% if stdlib_only %]
- **Standard library only:** no runtime dependency, ever (CI fails); the program file imports nothing from its own package.
- **Config:** arguments first. Environment variables are `[[ env_prefix ]]<KEY>`, read in one place; a file, if any, is TOML (`tomllib`); the precedence is on In-Depth-Configuration.
- **Errors:** specific exceptions; a usage error is one line and exits with `EXIT_USAGE` (2 unless the program declares another, and the project's design record says why). No bare `except:`.
[% elif has_cli %]
- **Config:** every setting through `config.SETTINGS`: `[[ env_prefix ]]<KEY>_FILE` > `[[ env_prefix ]]<KEY>` > file > default. Secrets: `secret=True`, from `_FILE`, never logged. A secret is a `Secret`: `.reveal()` where it's used; `str()` gives `********`.
- **Errors:** specific exceptions; the CLI prints one line and exits 2. No bare `except:`.
[% endif %]
[% if stdlib_only %]
- **Dependencies:** dev only (`uv add --dev`).
[% else %]
- **Dependencies:** only when the stdlib or an existing one can't; justify it, and check the name exists.
[% endif %]
- **Tests:** each behaviour change gets a test that fails without it; no network in unit tests.
- **Never:** edit `CHANGELOG.md`, the version or generated wiki blocks; lower the coverage floor or skip a test; add `no-docs-needed` (reviewers only), telemetry or import-time network calls.

## Definition of done

`sh scripts/checks.sh` (wiki standard, version, lock), then `uv run ruff check && uv run ruff format --check`, `uv run mypy`, `uv run pytest`, `uv run scripts/gen-wiki.py --check`[% if stdlib_only %], `uv run scripts/check-stdlib.py`[% endif %][% if container_image or contrib %], `scripts/check-manifests.sh`[% endif %]; with Docker, `scripts/check-markdown.sh`. And your change's docs-map pages.

## Docs map

| You changed | Update |
|---|---|
[% if stdlib_only %]
| an argument, a command, an input | In-Depth-Configuration, CLI-Reference |
[% elif has_cli %]
| a setting, a command | In-Depth-Configuration, CLI-Reference (regenerate) |
[% endif %]
[% if kind == 'service' %]
| a route | HTTP-API-Reference (regenerate, then document) |
[% endif %]
[% if kind == 'library' %]
| the public API | API-Reference |
[% endif %]
[% if contrib %]
| `Dockerfile`, `contrib/**` | Deployment |
[% endif %]
| components; security; a failure mode; tests | Architecture-Internals (+ a record); Security; Troubleshooting; Testing-Guide |

Wiki links use page names (`[Quick Start](Quick-Start)`); link new pages from `_Sidebar.md`.
